# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in the value. That copy is yours and
# is not committed; this template is what the repository carries.
#
# Only secrets live here. Everything else this Worker reads is in
# `wrangler.toml`, so no name appears in both files and nothing overrides
# anything.

# The same string as INGEST_SHARED_SECRET in the repo-root `.env`, and the same
# one `wrangler secret put INGEST_SHARED_SECRET --env production` sets on the
# deployed Worker. The server signs upload tickets with it and this Worker
# verifies them, so a mismatch rejects every upload with 401.
# Generate one with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
INGEST_SHARED_SECRET=

# Optional: the private key that opens the model keys a web-animation run
# fetches from the server before each model call (RSA-OAEP-256, PKCS#8 PEM).
# The server holds the matching public key as INGEST_KEY_SEAL_PUBLIC_KEY; keys
# are opened in memory for that one call and never stored here. Without it, a
# web-animation submit answers 501 feature_disabled. Generate the pair as
# `.env.dev` describes. On a deployment:
# `wrangler secret put KEY_UNSEAL_PRIVATE_KEY --env production`.
KEY_UNSEAL_PRIVATE_KEY=
